content.internal/analysis/specs/numbers.json:
{
  "name": "numbers",
  "kind": "go",
  "class": "free",
  "maxTurns": 0,
  "description": "Does exact arithmetic and figure handling over the matter's verified figures, so no model ever computes or types a number. op \"calc\" runs fn (sum, diff, ratio, pct, product, date_add, date_diff, business_days) over operands that are verified finding values, written {\"ref\": \"F12.v1\"} exactly as ledger and extraction results show them, or literals with a unit (\"21\" with unit \"days\", \"2026-11-12\" with unit \"date\", \"35\" with unit \"%\"), and returns a worksheet with an id (wid); drafters write it as the handle {wid} (e.g. {W1a2b3c4d5e}) and Go renders its result, so every total, recalculated amount and computed date in the deliverable must be such a worksheet. product multiplies (a percentage counts as its fraction: 35% of a $100,000 shortfall is $35,000); date_add and business_days take a negative count to count back from an event; date_add with holidays set (even []) rolls a result that lands on a weekend or one of those holidays to the next day that is not (backward for a negative count), as FRCP 6(a) does, and the worksheet shows the raw date. op \"handles\" gives each verified figure of fids (all when null) a codename such as {Zephyr} that keeps its figure for the whole run; drafters write the codename and the renderer substitutes the exact value. op \"table\" returns a Markdown key-figures table built only from verified values. handles and table return one page of about 12 KB (whole items, whole rows): when the result says truncated, call again naming fewer fids for the rest. Do not use it to estimate, round or infer a figure the record does not state, and do not use a quarantined finding's value: it is refused, never treated as zero.\nExample: {\"op\": \"calc\", \"fn\": \"product\", \"operands\": [{\"ref\": \"F3.v1\", \"literal\": null, \"unit\": null}, {\"ref\": null, \"literal\": \"35\", \"unit\": \"%\"}], \"holidays\": null, \"fids\": null, \"salientTop\": null}\nExample: {\"op\": \"calc\", \"fn\": \"date_add\", \"operands\": [{\"ref\": \"F12.v1\", \"literal\": null, \"unit\": null}, {\"ref\": null, \"literal\": \"21\", \"unit\": \"days\"}], \"holidays\": [\"2026-11-11\", \"2026-11-26\"], \"fids\": null, \"salientTop\": null}\nExample: {\"op\": \"handles\", \"fn\": null, \"operands\": null, \"holidays\": null, \"fids\": null, \"salientTop\": 12}",
  "in": {
    "type": "object", "additionalProperties": false,
    "required": ["op", "fn", "operands", "holidays", "fids", "salientTop"],
    "properties": {
      "op": {"type": "string", "enum": ["calc", "handles", "table"]},
      "fn": {"type": ["string", "null"], "enum": ["sum", "diff", "ratio", "pct", "product", "date_add", "date_diff", "business_days", null]},
      "operands": {"type": ["array", "null"], "maxItems": 50, "items": {
